From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Yates <jonjryjo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:00:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] thunderbolt: stream: Add zero-copy progress diagnostics

The DS4-shaped asymmetric workload can stop making progress without
enough state to distinguish a fabric delivery failure from a missed
interrupt, ring harvest, or stream event publication failure.

Add lock-consistent NHI ring counters and snapshots, a privileged and
explicitly enabled diagnostic work kick, and zero-copy stream counters
exposed through a compat-stable UAPI. Preserve the first terminal error,
make FIFO and descriptor errors fail explicitly, and retain queued events
for reaping before EIO.

Also make partial RX repost failures transactional and report TX drain,
CLOSE, and path-disable failures with stable device identifiers.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Yates <jonjryjo@gmail.com>
---
